  "pr": {
    "body": "The production CLI wraps PHREEQC in Phase and Displacement adapters, but SolverStack and Phase hide its explicit trusted readback capability. Forward a unique opted-in aqueous adapter through those wrappers; refuse generic and ambiguous providers and preserve optional partial answers without issuing a receipt.\n\nAdd four core regression groups and the maintained native mechanical acceptance suite through the exact CLI wrapper topology. Characterization does not certify full-stack chemistry/phase/route acceptance, and this change installs no haloalkane reaction.\n\nIndependent source review and rustfmt/diff checks pass. Draft pending hosted compile, native/cache-only/Wasm compatibility and full applicable own fleet. No local Cargo, native or browser execution under resource gates. See `crates/kerotakis-core/TRUSTED-STACK-AQUEOUS-READBACK.md`.\n",
